Ask the backend whether it is up and print what it reports about itself: its address, status and version, any other detail it shares, and how long it took to answer.
Needs no connection, token or passphrase, and changes nothing. Use it to tell a server problem from a local one.

Usage: agent-cli server

Flags:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -v, --verbose  Print diagnostic details to stderr

Examples:
  agent-cli server
  $env:THE_AGENT_CLI_API_URL = "https://agent.example.com"; agent-cli server

Environment: THE_AGENT_CLI_API_URL, THE_AGENT_CLI_HOME
Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 unhealthy or unreachable server · 2 usage error or invalid API URL · 6 rate limited
